    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "7 Miles Out"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Carol Morley (Dreams of a Life, The Falling) adapts her moving semi-autobiographical novel, capturing her adolescence in Stockport during the 70s and 80s."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/hot-water-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Hot Water"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This atmospheric and sharply funny road movie sees a Lebanese mother and her American son take a trip, with a lot to unpack along the way."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/josephine-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Josephine"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Winner of the Grand Jury Dramatic Prize at Sundance, this suspenseful and devastating film follows a child trying to navigate life after witnessing a sexual assault."
    }
  ]
